@startuml fig_lease_vs_fence
!include _style.puml
' Book figure — why a lease is not a fence. Form: sequence, two panels.
' Evidence status: conceptual illustration — it draws the mechanism the fill-lease
' and publication-fence cards describe (v2-15) and asserts no rate.
title a lease can expire; a fencing token cannot be outrun

participant "filler R1" as R1
participant "fill lease" as L
participant "cache" as C

group lease alone: the old filler may still publish
  R1 -> L : acquire lease #7
  note over R1 : slow source read
  L --> L : lease #7 expires
  L -> C : lease #8 issued to a second filler
  C -> C : that filler publishes S1
  R1 -> C : publish S0 (its lease has lapsed)
  note over C : a lease cannot reject this
end

group lease with a fencing token: the old filler is rejected
  R1 -> L : acquire token 7
  L -> C : token 7
  L -> C : token 8 issued later
  C -> C : publish(token 8) — accepted
  R1 -> C : publish(token 7) — rejected
  note over C : the source generation rejects it
end
@enduml
